   "why": "At t=1 Adam's bias correction makes m_hat = g and v_hat = g^2, so the update is lr*g/(|g|+eps) = +/- lr for every parameter with a non-zero gradient. The gradient's MAGNITUDE cancels out entirely; only its sign survives. The first Adam step is a jump of size lr in a direction estimated from one batch.",
